    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0590" n="492" xml:id="pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/470b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-11T17:00:00-05:00">December 11, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>428. For the Minister: The Department’s 419, December 8, 5 p.m.<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d538-f1"/></p>
                <p>Department has been informed by Minister Wu that a copy of the Chinese
                    Government’s counter proposals, as presented to the Department by Minister Wu on
                    December 7, has been handed to you. Please telegraph the differences between the
                    text thereof and the text of the counter proposals handed, as reported by
                        you,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d538-f2"/> to the British Minister on December
                    1.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
